James wrote:
> Wouldn't it be best to carry a maximum of unneeded items (like
> gems) around in your open inventory?  From what I understand,
> the curse will choose an item from your open inventory at
> random, and every time it chooses a gem, it doesn't choose your
> weapon, armor or bag of holding.

I've seen this suggested before (don't remember where). You are correct, 
the spell chooses a random number of curses and spreads them out 
randomly amongst your inventory (it is possible the same item will be 
affected more than once) - see rndcurse() in sit.c. The more junk items 
you have, the less likely it is that something you care about will be hit.

I can't say that this is something that's ever been a particular issue 
for me however.

If you choose to do this, I would suggest keeping a few open inventory 
slots, for getting things out of your BoH, picking up footrice corpses etc.

This trick won't protect your steed's saddle, which has a separate - and 
usually much higher - 1/4 chance of being affected.


